# Purpose

This file imports the raw **Still Face event log exports** (one Excel file per
subject, produced by the video-coding software), identifies the Baseline /
Still Face / Reunion episode boundaries for each subject, and produces two
output datasets: a **raw** dataset (the labeled, un-scored event data, one row
per coded behavior instance) and a **computed** dataset (one row per subject,
every duration/count/proportion score from the **6M Still Face Score Sheet
(v2)**, with SPSS variable labels attached). See Section 7 for why these are
kept separate and saved to different files.

# 1. Setup

## Update the file path

**This is the main section a new user should edit.** Replace only the
user-specific portion of `PROJECT_ROOT` with the location of the Still Face
event log folder on your computer (OneDrive or Box, depending on where the
study ends up storing these).

**Example (OneDrive):**
`"C:/Users/abc1234/OneDrive - The Pennsylvania State University/Still Face"`

Use **forward slashes** in the path, including on Windows.

```{r setup, include=FALSE}
knitr::opts_chunk$set(echo = TRUE, message = FALSE, warning = FALSE)
```

```{r file-paths}
# EDIT THIS LINE: replace the user-specific portion with your own file location.
